Third-party references:
- OpenHarmony communication_dsoftbus (Apache License 2.0): FDEE service UUID used
  as a cross-reference for the beacon format.
- Wire formats were learned through interoperability analysis (Directive 2009/24/EC,
  Article 6). No vendor code is included.
- LibrePods (https://github.com/librepods-org/librepods, GPL-3.0, commit
  929a5358c62ce1fc66fa63200d77eab872a07507): Android UI components, theme and
  quick-settings patterns, imported and modified.
  No LibrePods media (videos, images, AirPods artwork) or fonts are included.
  The connection island is also imported from LibrePods and modified:
  android/app/src/main/java/io/github/librebuds/overlay/IslandWindow.kt,
  res/layout/island_window.xml, res/drawable/island_*.xml and
  res/drawable/ic_undo_button_bg.xml. Where LibrePods plays its AirPods clip, the island
  shows the LibreBuds product render of the model. The case-open popup window is imported the same
  way and modified: android/app/src/main/java/io/github/librebuds/popup/PopupWindow.kt;
  its layout (res/layout/popup_window.xml) is written for LibreBuds.
- res/drawable/ic_undo.xml: Material Symbols icon path (Google, Apache License 2.0).
- Material Symbols icon paths (Google, Apache License 2.0), via LibrePods'
  presentation/MaterialIcons.kt (android/app/.../ui/icons/MaterialIcons.kt), plus the
  "nearby" path added there and res/drawable/ic_mode_off.xml, ic_mode_cancellation.xml and
  ic_mode_awareness.xml.
- Product renders and launcher artwork (res/drawable-nodpi/battery_*.webp, thumb_*.webp,
  res/drawable-night-nodpi/*.webp, res/mipmap-*/ic_launcher_foreground.webp, and the
  vectors derived from them: res/drawable/ic_launcher_monochrome.xml and ic_buds.xml):
  LibreBuds original artwork generated with an image model; no third-party licence. The
  launcher background (res/drawable/ic_launcher_background.xml) is a plain gradient.
- Inter typeface (SIL Open Font License 1.1), loaded at runtime through Google Fonts.
- Case animations (android/app/src/main/res/raw/popup_*.mp4): LibreBuds original artwork generated
  with image and video models.
